Enhancement: lock parity Phase 6 local graduation gates

Vaultic now has OS-process locking tests in addition to in-process race tests.
They cover concurrent append backups and a backup racing a retrying
minimal-lock prune, with a final repository check. Durable prune-plan recovery
also verifies that a crash/interruption after the phase-A exclusive claim clears
only the pending marker and does not delete data.

The locking roadmap records these completed local gates and explicitly leaves
MinIO/S3 eventual-consistency, destructive cross-process, mixed-client, and
long-running soak gates pending before any Alpha behavior is promoted.

